PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Colleagues 5, 7 and 14 have already highlighted the key constraint that standard translation requires an AUG initiation codon, which immediately rules out the continuous SCFPTNSFFCHG frame advanced by colleagues 1/9/13. That frame, while it can be obtained by direct T→U substitution on the supplied forward strand, begins without any start codon and therefore cannot represent the first protein produced under conventional ribosome-scanning rules.  

At the same time, the MAKEAIGREAT reading rests on an unstated premise that the given 5′→3′ forward sequence must be treated as the template strand—an assumption the problem statement never supplies. The wording explicitly labels the sequence “forward DNA” without any template qualifier, so the default textbook convention treats it as the coding strand. Under that convention the mRNA is produced by simple T→U substitution, the sole in-frame AUG occurs at nucleotides 32–34, and the only AUG-initiated peptide recoverable from the fragment is the Met-Gly dipeptide MG.  

This keeps the answer strictly inside the wording provided while satisfying the biological requirement for initiation. The split between the two forward-strand interpretations (SCFPTNSFFCHG versus MG) is therefore the only division that remains consistent with the problem’s explicit phrasing; any move toward MAKEAIGREAT would require adding an extra interpretive step the text does not authorize.}

